        "original_id": "056c77c8-e38f-5c68-83d2-b0f8913e4ff9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Die Macher, ZÈRTZ\n- People: Karl-Heinz Schmiel\n- Projects: GIPF Project\n- Concepts: German electoral system, political parties\n\nFacts:\n- Die Macher is a strategy board game designed by Karl-Heinz Schmiel of Germany.\n- Die Macher is based on the German electoral system.\n- In Die Macher, each player takes the role of one of five political parties.\n- In the 2006 edition of Die Macher, the five political parties are the CDU/CSU, FDP, SPD, Greens, and Die Linke.\n- ZÈRTZ is the third game in the GIPF Project.\n- The GIPF Project is a set of six abstract strategy games.",
